.Dd $Mdocdate: October 28 2026 $
.Dt PROTON-OPENBSD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm proton-openbsd
.Nd run 64-bit Windows programs with Proton's wine, DXVK and vkd3d-proton
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm run
.Ar program.exe
.Op Ar arg ...
.Nm
.Ar wine-program
.Op Ar arg ...
.Nm
.Cm prefix
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sets up a wine prefix and runs a Windows program in it the way Valve's
Proton does, using Proton's fork of wine
.Pq Pa ${TRUEPREFIX}/lib/proton-wine ,
DXVK for Direct3D 9, 10 and 11, and vkd3d-proton for Direct3D 12.
.Pp
On every start the DLLs selected below are copied into the prefix's
.Pa drive_c/windows/system32
if they differ, and
.Ev WINEDLLOVERRIDES
is set so that wine loads them instead of its builtin versions.
DXVK provides d3d9, d3d10core, d3d11 and dxgi; vkd3d-proton provides d3d12
and d3d12core; wine's own wined3d provides d3d8.
If DXVK or vkd3d-proton is not installed, wine's builtin DLLs are used for
those APIs.
Wine's fonts, and any fonts in
.Ev PROTON_FONTS_DIR ,
are linked into the prefix's
.Pa drive_c/windows/Fonts ,
where Proton's wine expects the system fonts.
.Pp
ICU 68
.Pq textproc/proton-icu ,
which wine's icu.dll forwards to and which programs built on .NET 5 or
later need, is linked into
.Pa system32
as well.
.Pp
If
.Ev SteamAppId
is set, as
.Xr proton-launcher 1
does for Steam games, the program runs under
.Pa C:\eProgram Files (x86)\eSteam\esteam.exe
from proton-steamclient.
It registers itself as the running Steam client and
.Pa steamclient64.dll
as its library, so that the game's Steamworks API
.Pq steam_api64.dll
starts.
The library answers for the account proton-launcher logged in with,
and keeps stats, achievements and cloud files under
.Ev PROTON_STEAM_USERDATA .
Online features such as lobbies and the workshop are not available.
.Pp
The soft limits on data size and open files are raised to the hard
limits of the login class, since the
.Dq staff
class allows only 1.5 GB of data by default.
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm run Ar program.exe Op Ar arg ...
Run a Windows program.
.It Ar wine-program Op Ar arg ...
Run a program shipped with wine, such as
.Cm winecfg ,
.Cm regedit
or
.Cm wineboot ,
in the same prefix and with the same settings.
.It Cm prefix
Create the prefix, or update the DLLs in it, and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PROTON_PREFIX
The wine prefix to use.
Defaults to
.Ev WINEPREFIX
if set, otherwise
.Pa ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}/proton-openbsd/pfx .
.It Ev PROTON_FONTS_DIR
Additional directory of
.Pa .ttf
and
.Pa .ttc
fonts to link into the prefix, such as the fonts Proton builds from
Liberation, Noto and Source Han.
Defaults to
.Pa ${TRUEPREFIX}/share/proton-fonts .
.It Ev PROTON_USE_WINED3D
If non-zero, use wine's OpenGL-based wined3d for all Direct3D versions
instead of DXVK and vkd3d-proton.
.It Ev PROTON_DXVK_D3D8
If non-zero, also use DXVK's d3d8.
.It Ev PROTON_NO_D3D11 , PROTON_NO_D3D10
If non-zero, disable Direct3D 11, or Direct3D 10, as Proton does.
.It Ev PROTON_NO_STEAM
Run Steam games without steam.exe and steamclient64.dll.
.It Ev PROTON_STEAM_TRACE
Log the calls the game makes into steamclient64.dll to standard error.
.It Ev PROTON_NO_FSYNC
If non-zero, do not use fsync, the futex-based in-process implementation
of Windows synchronization objects; every wait then goes through
.Xr wineserver 1 .
.It Ev WINE_PRECISE_SLEEP
The system clock ticks at 100 Hz, so a sleep ends on a tick after its
timeout.
Programs that ask for a finer timer resolution
.Pq Fn timeBeginPeriod
sleep precisely, by sleeping in the kernel for whole ticks and yielding
the processor for the rest; 1 forces this for all programs, 0 turns it
off.
.It Ev PROTON_LOG
If 1, append a log with Proton's default wine debug channels and DXVK and
vkd3d-proton messages to
.Pa proton- Ns Ar program Ns Pa .log
in
.Ev PROTON_LOG_DIR
(default:
.Ev HOME ) .
Any other non-zero value is added to the default
.Ev WINEDEBUG
channels.
.It Ev LC_CTYPE
If the current locale's character set is not UTF-8,
.Nm
sets
.Ev LC_CTYPE
to
.Dq C.UTF-8
(or
.Ev LC_ALL ,
if that is set),
so that Windows file names with non-ASCII characters map to Unix names.
.It Ev WINEDLLOVERRIDES
Appended after the overrides set by
.Nm ,
so user settings take precedence.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run a game with DXVK, logging to
.Pa ~/proton-game.log :
.Pp
.Dl $ PROTON_LOG=1 proton-openbsd run ~/games/game/game.exe
.Pp
Configure the prefix:
.Pp
.Dl $ proton-openbsd winecfg
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wine 1
.Sh CAVEATS
Only 64-bit Windows programs can run on
.Ox ;
the kernel provides no 32-bit code segment for user processes.
.Nm
refuses to start 32-bit executables with an explanation.
Many installers of 64-bit programs are themselves 32-bit; use the
program's
.Pa .msi
package (with
.Ic proton-openbsd msiexec /i file.msi )
or a portable archive instead.
DXVK and vkd3d-proton need a Vulkan driver, which on
.Ox
means Mesa's anv or radv on Intel or AMD graphics.
Steam, Steam's runtime and anti-cheat systems are not supported.
.Pp
Sound goes through wine's PulseAudio driver: the PulseAudio client
library starts a
.Xr pulseaudio 1
daemon on demand, which plays through
.Xr sndiod 8 .
If programs are silent, check that
.Ic pactl info
reports a default sink.
On machines without audio hardware a null sink keeps programs that wait
for audio running:
.Ic pulseaudio -n --daemonize=yes --load=module-null-sink --load=module-native-protocol-unix .
.Pp
Without the proton-wine-addons package (Wine Mono and Wine Gecko),
.Nm
disables mscoree and mshtml, and programs that need .NET or wine's HTML
engine do not work.
